From e60fd5ac1f6851be5b2c042b39584bfcf8a66f57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caleb Connolly <caleb@connolly.tech>
Date: Sun, 2 May 2021 01:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-oneplus-common: guard rmtfs-mem

The rmtfs_mem region is a weird one, downstream allocates it
dynamically, and supports a "qcom,guard-memory" property which when set
will reserve 4k above and below the rmtfs memory.

A common from qcom 4.9 kernel msm_sharedmem driver:

/*
 * If guard_memory is set, then the shared memory region
 * will be guarded by SZ_4K at the start and at the end.
 * This is needed to overcome the XPU limitation on few
 * MSM HW, so as to make this memory not contiguous with
 * other allocations that may possibly happen from other
 * clients in the system.
*/

When the kernel tries to touch memory that is too close the
rmtfs region it may cause an XPU violation. Such is the case on the
OnePlus 6 where random crashes would occur usually after boot.

Reserve 4k above and below the rmtfs_mem to avoid hitting these XPU
Violations.

This doesn't entirely solve the random crashes on the OnePlus 6/6T but
it does seem to prevent the ones which happen shortly after modem
bringup.

Fixes: 288ef8a42612 ("arm64: dts: sdm845: add oneplus6/6t devices")
Signed-off-by: Caleb Connolly <caleb@connolly.tech>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20210502014146.85642-4-caleb@connolly.tech
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <bjorn.andersson@linaro.org>
---
Source: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/e60fd5ac1f6851be5b2c042b39584bfcf8a66f57
Local adaptation for Polaris on Linux 7.3:
- Apply the SDM845 XPU guard policy to Polaris, whose downstream SDM845 DT
  also requires qcom,guard-memory.
- Use the current qcom,use-guard-pages binding instead of separate nodes.
  Reserve 4 KiB on each side while keeping the existing RMTFS payload at
  0xf6301000 with size 0x200000. No firmware/calibration data is changed.
- Downstream reference: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sdm845/blob/aa8adfe9bf212c6e93238a86980b4024da4f819a/drivers/uio/msm_sharedmem/msm_sharedmem.c#L151
The original commit message and trailers above describe the OnePlus change;
Polaris validation confirms the unchanged effective payload address/size,
non-overlapping reservations, modem startup and WLAN scanning. The guards
alone did not resolve the separate modem shutdown reset.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
@@ -103,10 +103,11 @@
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		rmtfs_mem: memory@f6301000 {
+		rmtfs_mem: memory@f6300000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,rmtfs-mem";
-			reg = <0 0xf6301000 0 0x200000>;
-			no-map;
+			reg = <0 0xf6300000 0 0x202000>;
+			no-map;
+			qcom,use-guard-pages;
 
 			qcom,client-id = <1>;
 			qcom,vmid = <QCOM_SCM_VMID_MSS_MSA>;
